{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Anecdotes and Personal Stories"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Childhood Lessons"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe situations in written and spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le12ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing <span class=\"italic\">You</span> and <span class=\"italic\">I</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You stress <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">you</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I</span></span> to add meaning and emphasis to a statement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you stress a word, you make it longer, louder and a little higher tone. You can put stress on a word to emphasize it and make your meaning clearer. <br/>You stress <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">you</span></span> or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">I</span></span> when you want to emphasize something about a person that is not expected."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'm good. But how about <span class=\"strong\">you</span>?</span><ul><li>When you put stress on <span class=\"strong\">you</span>, you shift the emphasis to the other person.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read these sentences with stress on the bolded words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Well ... maybe <span class=\"strong\">I</span> was much more gullible than <span class=\"strong\">you</span> were.</li><li>I don't know about <span class=\"strong\">you</span>, but <span class=\"strong\">I</span> believed them all! </li><li><span class=\"strong\">I</span> always wear a sweater. Do <span class=\"strong\">you</span>?</li><li>As an adult, <span class=\"strong\">I</span> no longer believe in easy answers. What about <span class=\"strong\">you</span>? </span></li></ul>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Intonation of Finished and Unfinished Ideas"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Intonation tells us a lot about how someone feels and whether they have completed their thoughts or not. It is important to listen carefully to the rise and fall of people's voices. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, there there are three intonation patterns:<ol><li>Falling</li><li>Rising</li><li>Partial Falling </li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You should use falling intonation at the end of a thought group or sentence to tell the listener that you are finished with that statement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Most people just make promises without paying too much attention to what they are saying.  </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Likewise, your  pitch will only partially fall at the end of a thought group to:<ul><li>give the listener's brain time to \u201cdigest\u201d the speech; and</li><li>tell the listener that you are not finished speaking.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Well ... I have to tell you ... </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you want to convince me of something ... to persuade me with a catchy phrase ... think again. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's the honest truth ... I promise!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well ... maybe I was much more gullible than you were. I believed everything!"}, {"type": "example", "content": " I mean ... remember when you were small ... people made lots of promises."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pay attention "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to focus on something or someone without distraction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People just make promises without paying too much attention to what they are saying."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about promises."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gullible "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easy to deceive; easily believes everything other people say"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Maybe I was much more gullible than you were."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "zealously "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "done eagerly and with enthusiasm "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I ate my spinach zealously."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "robust "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "strong and healthy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was never what you'd call robust."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to intone "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say something slowly and seriously in a voice which does not rise or fall much"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: \"If you wear a sweater, you won't catch a cold,\" my mom lovingly intoned all winter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to come down with"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to catch or show signs of an illness"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I always come down with a cold in the winter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to ascertain "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to discover something, or to make sure of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It took me several years to ascertain that practice wasn't a magic formula."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "despite "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without being influenced or prevented by"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(preposition)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I always feel especially good despite promises which had nothing to do with reality"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "life's lessons "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "experiences from which useful knowledge or principles can be learned"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Despite life's lessons showing me that it's hard to work with others, I always feel especially good after playing basketball with my friends."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "That's the honest truth!"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to express deep sincerity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's the honest truth ...  I promise!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob04aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library and look up the lyrics to the song <span class=\"italic\">Promises, Promises</span> written by Burt Bacharach."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read through them and say the lyrics aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now go find someone singing the song online or on CD at the library."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen without reading the lyrics the first time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go back to the lyrics and highlight words that you didn't hear or that were hard to hear."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen again with the lyric sheet."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find the lyrics and song to <span class=\"italic\">Promises, Promises</span> written by Burt Bacharach."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read through the lyrics then listen to the song."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I note any words that were difficult to hear."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to the song again with the lyrics sheet."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about friendship, relationships, feelings and reactions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can stress <span class=\"italic\">I</span> and <span class=\"italic\">you</span>."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can use proper intonation in finished and unfinished ideas."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How often do you make promises?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you always keep your promises? Why or why not?"}]}, 